@page "/admin-settings"

<PageTitle>Admin Settings - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<PageHero Eyebrow="OPERATIONSFLOW / ADMINISTRATION"
          Title="Admin Settings"
          Subtitle="Admin Settings shows the configuration surface OperationsFlow would need before production rollout. The current app runs in local demo mode, but Week 3 now documents the storage provider path and Week 4 will add production authentication and permissions."
          BadgeText="Readiness Surface"
          BadgeClass="of-badge of-badge-info">
    <Actions>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/technical-overview">Technical Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/integration-overview">Integration Overview</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-secondary" href="/user-roles">User Roles</a>
        <a class="of-btn of-btn-primary" href="/document-library">Document Library</a>
    </Actions>
</PageHero>

<PurposeNote Title="Purpose" Icon="⚙️">
    <p>
        This page documents the current local configuration and the production settings OperationsFlow will need for SharePoint storage,
        Microsoft Entra ID authentication, role enforcement, audit behaviour, notifications, and reporting.
    </p>
</PurposeNote>

<MetricGrid>
    <MetricCard Title="Current Mode"
                Value="Local Demo"
                Detail="No production authentication or role enforcement active yet."
                Icon="💻"
                Tone="info" />

    <MetricCard Title="Storage Provider"
                Value="Local"
                Detail="Files are stored under wwwroot/uploads for development proof only."
                Icon="📁"
                Tone="success" />

    <MetricCard Title="Future Auth"
                Value="Entra ID"
                Detail="Week 4 target for login and role-aware access control."
                Icon="🔐"
                Tone="warning" />

    <MetricCard Title="Future Files"
                Value="SharePoint"
                Detail="Week 4 target for production document library storage."
                Icon="☁️"
                Tone="default" />
</MetricGrid>

<GuidanceNote Title="Current boundary" Icon="⚠️" Tone="warning">
    <p>
        These settings are a readiness surface. The current local app does not enforce production authentication,
        production role permissions, SharePoint storage, retention policies, or tenant-level security.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>

<TableCard Title="Current local evidence settings"
           Subtitle="These settings describe the working Week 3 local foundation.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Setting</th>
                <th>Current value</th>
                <th>Notes</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Application mode</span></td>
                <td>Local demo / portfolio prototype</td>
                <td>Used to prove workflow, not production security.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Database</span></td>
                <td>SQLite</td>
                <td>Stores workflow records, activity logs, and attachment metadata.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">File storage provider</span></td>
                <td>Local</td>
                <td>Files are stored locally under wwwroot/uploads.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Attachment metadata</span></td>
                <td>DocumentAttachment records</td>
                <td>Links files to module, record id, provider, file name, path/key, and status.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">File delete behaviour</span></td>
                <td>Soft delete metadata</td>
                <td>Deleted files are hidden from active library views and logged for traceability.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Activity audit</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log</td>
                <td>Upload/delete events are recorded for reviewer evidence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-danger">Git safety</span></td>
                <td>Do not commit uploads or database files</td>
                <td>wwwroot/uploads, *.db, *.db-shm, and *.db-wal must stay out of commits.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<div class="of-two-column-grid">
    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 storage settings needed"
               Subtitle="These settings will be needed before the SharePoint provider can replace the local provider."
               Tone="info">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Provider selector:</strong><span>Local or SharePoint.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Tenant id:</strong><span>Microsoft 365 tenant identifier.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Client id:</strong><span>App registration id.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Secret/certificate:</strong><span>Secure Graph authentication credential.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>SharePoint site:</strong><span>Host/site path or site id.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Drive/library:</strong><span>Drive id, library id, or document library name.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Base folder:</strong><span>Root folder path for OperationsFlow evidence.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Folder convention:</strong><span>Module and record id based evidence folders.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Upload controls:</strong><span>Allowed file types and size limits.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Retention:</strong><span>Archive, recycle, or retention-aligned delete behaviour.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>

    <InfoPanel Title="Week 4 auth/role settings needed"
               Subtitle="These settings support the move from local demo to production access control."
               Tone="warning">

        <ul class="of-mini-list">
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Auth provider:</strong><span>Microsoft Entra ID.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Role source:</strong><span>Entra groups, app roles, or local config mapping.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Admin:</strong><span>System configuration, provider setup, and role management.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Manager:</strong><span>Workflow oversight, reports, data quality, and follow-up review.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Reviewer:</strong><span>Evidence, reports, quality checks, and audit review.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Worker:</strong><span>Assigned work updates and evidence uploads.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>ReadOnly:</strong><span>View-only access for review and demonstration.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Policy mapping:</strong><span>Upload, delete, export, settings, and role management permissions.</span></li>
            <li class="of-mini-list-item"><strong>Dev fallback:</strong><span>Safe local testing mode if needed.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </InfoPanel>
</div>

<TableCard Title="Production setting groups"
           Subtitle="These are the major configuration groups needed for a production-ready OperationsFlow deployment.">

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Group</th>
                <th>Examples</th>
                <th>Production concern</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Storage</span></td>
                <td>Provider, site id, drive id, folder convention, file limits</td>
                <td>Files must be stored somewhere supportable, permissioned, and backed up.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Identity</span></td>
                <td>Tenant id, authority, client id, login policy</td>
                <td>Users should authenticate through Microsoft Entra ID, not local demo assumptions.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Authorization</span></td>
                <td>Roles, groups, app policies, permissions</td>
                <td>Not every user should delete files, change settings, export data, or manage roles.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Audit</span></td>
                <td>Activity Log retention, upload/delete events, record changes</td>
                <td>Operational systems need traceability for review and accountability.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Notifications</span></td>
                <td>Teams/Outlook alerts, Power Automate flows, reminder schedules</td>
                <td>Production systems should push important follow-up work to the right people.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Reporting</span></td>
                <td>CSV exports, Power BI dataset, scheduled reporting</td>
                <td>Managers need repeatable review outputs, not manual screenshot hunting.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</TableCard>

<InfoPanel Title="Week 4 admin implementation path"
           Subtitle="Admin Settings should move from a readiness page into real configurable production behaviour."
           Tone="success">

    <div class="of-review-proof-grid">
        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Step 1</span>
            <h3>Provider config</h3>
            <p>Add appsettings/user-secrets/environment variable support for Local vs SharePoint storage configuration.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Step 2</span>
            <h3>Auth config</h3>
            <p>Add Microsoft Entra ID settings and login setup without breaking local development testing.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Step 3</span>
            <h3>Role policy config</h3>
            <p>Map Admin, Manager, Reviewer, Worker, and ReadOnly roles to actual authorization policies.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="of-review-proof-card">
            <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Step 4</span>
            <h3>Deployment notes</h3>
            <p>Document the production values required before a real organisation could safely run the app.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Block 8 outcome" Icon="✅" Tone="info">
    <p>
        Admin Settings now clearly describes the current local provider and the configuration needed for the Week 4 SharePoint/Microsoft 365 production provider.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>